d a 2-year horizon, not 10 years, when illustrating outcomes to support the agreed risk level. This means the projection shown to the client to 'agree' the risk level did not model the stated investment term, which undermines the robustness of the risk level agreement process.\n\n5. Existing fund risk labels in file notes ([P11]) — Aviva 2, Zurich 7, Standard Life 4 — are Defaqto ratings for existing funds, not the client's ATR, and the file notes context makes this reasonably clear. These are not conflicting ATR scores.\n\n6. Vulnerability: No vulnerability flags are identified in the evidence that bear materially on this check.\n\nConclusion: The override from 4 to 5 is explained and acknowledged. The scale difference between KIID categories and advisory risk ratings is protected by the guard. However, the risk profile projection tool was run over 2 years when the stated investment term is 10 years — this is a material discrepancy that means the projection underpinning the agreed risk level was modelled on the wrong time horizon, casting doubt on whether the risk level agreement was properly informed. This is a Potential Concern at Moderate severity.","citations":[{"passageId":"P1","source":"D/Risk profile report.docx","category":"D","quote":"Your natural risk level is based on the answers given in the Attitude to Risk Questionnaire which was completed on 18/09/2025.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"D/Risk profile report.docx","category":"D","quote":null,"cells":["4  Cautious Balanced","As a Cautious Balanced investor you tend to see yourself as quite a cautious person and are inclined to view risk negatively rather than as a source of opportunity."]},{"passageId":"P12","source":"D/Risk profile report.docx","category":"D","quote":null,"cells":["5  Balanced","As a Balanced investor you do not see yourself as a particularly cautious person and have no strong positive or negative associations with the notion of taking risk."]},{"passageId":"P12","source":"D