mitment, the family benefit, the quarterly e-magazine, and online portfolio access. Most significantly, the report records review frequency as 'Unspecified', whereas the client agreement commits to 'at least annually'. The absence of a stated review frequency in the report means the client is not clearly informed of how often they will receive the service they are paying 1% per annum for. The guard notes that the client agreement and report may name services differently — the core services are recognisable across both documents. However, the omission of the annual review meeting commitment (the most material service element underpinning the ongoing charge) and the absence of review frequency in the report are genuine gaps, not mere labelling differences. The omission of the minimum fee is a minor point. There is no vulnerability information in the evidence that materially affects this assessment. The overall picture is that the charge rate is supported, but the service proposition as described in the report is thinner than what the client agreement commits to, and the lack of a stated review frequency is a specific gap for a client paying 1% pa on a pension fund of circa £110,000.","citations":[{"passageId":"P15","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":"Reviewing your attitude to risk and capacity for loss to ensure your investment portfolio remains suitable for you.\n Reviewing the ongoing suitability of your investment portfolio.\n Market updates and updates with any changes in financial legislation.\n Access to a professional, experienced and qualified team of financial advisers at any time to provide ad-hoc advice as required.\n Access to full holistic financial planning to suit your needs.\nThe costs for this service are 1% per annum. Based on current values & expected contributions, minus the initial fee, this would be equal to circa £1,101.85 for the first year.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P1","source":"TFAS Wealth Client Agreement Privacy.md","category":"A","quote":"ongoing annual review management charge of 1% (subject to a minimum fee of £100), which is automatically taken from the funds invested.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"IMPORT_2.md","category":"A","quote":"Review meeting at least once a year and recommendations which may include the following as part of this service; bed and ISA, fund switches, drawdown withdrawals, portfolio rebalance, updated fact find and attitude to risk. *\nStatements and Performance Reports twice per year.\nCash flow analysis when relevant and beneficial.\nFamily benefit where you can have an adviser fee free advice for direct family members for their ISA or pension set up on top of up to three hours advice for your children.\nRegular market updates.\nQuarterly e-magazine.\nOn-line access for portfolio valuations.\nAccess to your adviser should you need us in the meantime.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P2","source":"TFAS Wealth Client Agreement Privacy.md","category":"A","quote":"The fees you are required to pay for our advisory services are set out in the suitability report and any subsequent charges confirmation.","cells":null}],"severity":"Low","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

