cy between the narrative and the table label is a rounding artefact and does not affect the critical yield figures themselves; it is already recorded as an internal inconsistency and represents only a minor labelling difference.\n\nHowever, passage [P1] of the same pension switch report contains a different table — showing the same three plans switching to the same Aviva solution — but with the recommended RIY at only 0.6% (versus 2.1%–2.3% in the suitability report), critical yields of 0.3% / 3.2% / 6.0% (versus 1.9% / 4.8% / 7.8%), and effects of switching of only £2,000 / 1.9% (low), £2,000 / 1.6% (mid) and £3,000 / 2.0% (high). The earlier internal inconsistency note confirms that the suitability report separately shows a 'like-for-like' position of 0.24% cheaper and an 'including adviser fees' position of 4.24% more expensive. This strongly suggests that [P1] is the like-for-like (product/platform/investment charges only) version while [P2] is the including-adviser-fee version. The suitability report relies on and reproduces the [P2] figures. The existence of the [P1] table is material because a client reading the switch report appendix would encounter both tables without a clear signpost distinguishing them; the report itself does not explain why two different sets of critical yield / RIY / effect-of-switching figures appear in the same supporting document. The suitability report relies on the higher-cost (including adviser fee) scenario as its primary disclosure, which is correct, but the presence of the lower-cost table without reconciliation creates a material risk of client confusion and means the disclosure is not unambiguous.\n\nThe derived figures note that several charge percentages imply fund values referencing Zurich's current value rather than the plan actually labelled (EA5 / Standard Life), indicating that the underlying switch report calculation may have been run against the wrong base value for that plan. This affects the reliability of the RIY and critical yield comparison for Standard Life specifically.\n\nThe new Aviva illustration ([P13]) shows an all-charges RIY of 2.1% (real, at a 2.9% real growth rate), which is consistent with the recommended RIY at low growth in the report.\n\nVulnerability overlay: No specific vulnerability characteristics are recorded in the evidence that would materially change this assessment.\n\nIn summary: the report's core critical yield figures match the supporting switch report table in [P2]. However, the switch report also contains a second, materially different table ([P1]) that the suitability report does not acknowledge, reconcile or explain to the client. This is a Potential Concern of Moderate severity.","citations":[{"passageId":"P17","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Low growth rate - (0.00%)","Existing: £108,000 / 0.3%","New: £97,600 / 2.1% / 1.9% / £10,400 or 9.6% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["Mid growth rate - (2.95%)","Existing: £127,000 / 0.3%","New: £115,000 / 2.2% / 4.8% / £12,000 or 9.4% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P17","source":"Suitability Report Test 1.md","category":"I","quote":null,"cells":["High growth rate - (5.88%)","Existing: £150,000 / 0.3%","New: £135,000 / 2.3% / 7.8% / £15,000 or 10.0% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P2","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Low growth rate – (0.00%)","Existing RIY 0.3%","New RIY 2.1%","Critical yield 1.9%","Effect £10,400 or 9.6% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P2","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Mid growth rate – (2.95%)","Existing RIY 0.3%","New RIY 2.2%","Critical yield 4.8%","Effect £12,000 or 9.4% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P2","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["High growth rate – (5.88%)","Existing RIY 0.3%","New RIY 2.3%","Critical yield 7.8%","Effect 