tirement age (SRA). The charge is taken by reducing the number of capital units paid out; the charge reduces by around 0.3%-0.4% a month until SRA where there is no charge. The charge is capped at 1% from age 55.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P13","source":"Zurich Policy Info.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Transfer value and early retirement charge","This is the difference between current and transfer values.","There are no deductions taken from the current value if benefits are transferred or taken. The initial set up charges have already been paid."]},{"passageId":"P11","source":"Zurich Policy Info.md","category":"E","quote":null,"cells":["Personal payments regular","£0.00","Personal payments single","£0.00","Employer payments regular","£0.00","Employer payments single","£0.00","Former protected rights transfer payments","£2,344.58","Former protected rights payments","£12,419.11"]},{"passageId":"P16","source":"Standard_Life_Policy_Info.md","category":"E","quote":"No bid offer spread.\n100% allocation.\nNo loyalty bonus.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P16","source":"Standard_Life_Policy_Info.md","category":"E","quote":"For these contracts, if there was no block transfer, then there is definitely no Protected Tax Free Cash and the standard 25% will be available.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P20","source":"Test Case 1 - Policy Research -2025.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Market Value Reduction (MVR)?","No","No","n/a","n/a","No","No"]},{"passageId":"P22","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Mid growth rate – (2.95%)","Projected value at age 75 existing","£127,000","Projected value at age 75 new","£115,000","Critical yield","4.8%","Effect of switching","£12,000 or 9.4% decrease"]},{"passageId":"P22","source":"Pension switch report - updated.md","category":"G","quote":null,"cells":["Existing pension fund value at point of switching","£110,185.60"]},{"passageId":"P9","source":"Standard Life Policy illustr